 "id": "edit_boundary",
 "label": "Edit Boundary",
 "menu": null,
 "params": "{id, sketch?: [[[x,y],[x,y]],\u2026]} redraws a floor's, a ceiling's, a roof's footprint's or a shaft's outline and its holes (a floor's or a ceiling's openings, a roof's courtyards; a shaft has none) as a sketch, all at once (see `sketch`); a roof's gable edges stay gables where the new footprint has the same edge. Without `sketch`, gives the outline and holes it has now, as the lines to edit. The outline must be simple, as `floor` says; a line that crosses itself is found as two that cross are"
}
{
 "aliases": [],
 "id": "modify",
 "label": "Modify",
 "menu": null,
 "params": "{id | ids: [id,\u2026], \u2026fields} change fields as `elements` shows them, of one element or several; `level` and `top_level` may be names. A filled region's or a floor's model pattern is set by `pattern_origin` [x, y], plan mm, where its lines start, and `pattern_angle`, degrees counter-clockwise (both shown by `elements`); to put a pattern line of one on a reference line, Model::align_pattern gives the `pattern_origin` that does. A floor's, a ceiling's, a roof's or a shaft's outline it sets is held to what `floor` says of it"
}
{
 "aliases": [
  "AL"
 ],
 "id": "align",
 "label": "Align",
 "menu": null,
 "params": "{id, reference: [[x,y],[x,y]], line: [[x,y],[x,y]], lock?: true, to?: id} aligns an element's picked line with a reference in plan: turns by the smaller angle about the picked line's midpoint, then moves it onto the reference, keeping its size. Doors and windows slide along their host wall; they cannot turn independently. With `lock`, Revit's padlock: the line and the reference (of element `to`, else whatever has a line along it) are kept on one line after every command, as a locked dimension keeps its length; refused when that can't hold with the other locks. Returns {aligned, angle, by, line} (the picked line where it went), and the lock's id"
}
{
 "aliases": [
  "MV"
 ],
 "id": "move",
 "label": "Move",
 "menu": null,
 "params": "{ids: [id,\u2026], by: [dx, dy], end?: start|end} moves elements in plan; walls joined to a moved wall stretch to stay joined, and doors and windows slide along their walls. With `end`, only that end of one wall moves"
}
{
 "aliases": [
  "CO"
 ],
 "id": "copy",
 "label": "Copy",
 "menu": null,
 "params": "{ids: [id,\u2026], by: [dx, dy]} copies elements, with the doors and windows of copied walls; returns the copies' ids"
}
{
